        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioner David Dubin was convicted of healthcare fraud under 18 U. S. C. \u00a7 1347 after he overbilled Medicaid for psychological testing performed by the company he helped manage."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-22-10",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd608b26387f3e95842727f879e7c8ae6197059dca88b53e669a28622230f8c9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd608b26387f-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Argued February 27, 2023\u2014Decided June 8, 2023"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-22-10",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd608b26387f3e95842727f879e7c8ae6197059dca88b53e669a28622230f8c9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd608b26387f-0000-0006",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 1028A(a)(1) carries a severe penalty: a mandatory minimum sentence of two years in prison \u201cin addition to the punishment\u201d for the predicate offense."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-22-10",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd608b26387f3e95842727f879e7c8ae6197059dca88b53e669a28622230f8c9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd608b26387f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In sum, \u00a7 1028A(a)(1)'s title and text are mutually reinforc-\ning. Both point toward requiring the means of identifcation\nto be at the crux of the criminality."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-22-10",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd608b26387f3e95842727f879e7c8ae6197059dca88b53e669a28622230f8c9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd608b26387f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So long as the criteria for the broad predicate offenses are met, the Government's reading creates an automatic 2-year sentence for generic overbilling that happens to use ubiquitous payment methods."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-22-10",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd608b26387f3e95842727f879e7c8ae6197059dca88b53e669a28622230f8c9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd608b26387f-0002-0002",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Whoever among you is not an \u201caggravated identity thief,\u201d let him cast the frst stone. The United States came to this Court with a view of 18 U. S. C. \u00a7 1028A(a)(1) that would affx that unfortunate label on almost every adult American."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-22-10",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd608b26387f3e95842727f879e7c8ae6197059dca88b53e669a28622230f8c9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd608b26387f-0002-0003",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When, exactly, is a \u201cmeans of identifcation\u201d \u201cat the crux,\u201d \u201ca key mover,\u201d or a \u201ccentral role\u201d player in an offense? No doubt, the answer \u201cturns on causation, or at least causation often helps to answer the question.\u201d United States v. Michael, 882 F. 3d 624, 628 (CA6 2018). The Court agrees but stresses that \u201ca causal relationship\u201d of any kind will not suffce. Ante, at 131."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-22-10",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd608b26387f3e95842727f879e7c8ae6197059dca88b53e669a28622230f8c9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd608b26387f-0003-0000",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I do not write this opinion as wishcasting. Perhaps, by applying the Court's \u201ccrux\u201d test, lower courts will achieve a consistency that has, to date, eluded them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Reporter",
      "case_id": "2022-22-10",
